<title>USA: MBIA qualifies 13 muni bond issue for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies 13 muni bond issue for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp on Tuesday said it qualified for bond insurance the following 13 municipal issues slated for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Washington Elementary School District #6, Ariz., School Improvement, $34.825 million.</p>
<p>--Denver City &amp; County, Colo., Certificates of Participation, $39.955 million, direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Danbury, Conn., General Obligations (GOs), $10.1 million.</p>
<p>--Clinton Prairie School, Ind., Mortgage bonds, $1.9 million.</p>
<p>--Kansas Development Fin., Revenues, $6.48 million.</p>
<p>--Louisville Parking Authority, Ken., Mortgage Revenue Refunding,  direct purchase, $30.61 million.</p>
<p>--Gloucester, Mass., GOs, $14.575 million.</p>
<p>--Marion, Mass., Municipal Purpose Loan, $1.795 million.</p>
<p>--Zebulon, N.C., Water &amp; Sewer, $2.94 million.</p>
<p>--Park Ridge, N.J., General Improvment, $2.935 million.</p>
<p>--Corning City, N.Y., School District, $3.5 million.</p>
<p>--Rockland County, N.Y., GOs, $19.806 million.</p>
<p>--Hohenwald, Tenn., Public Imporvement, $2.3 million.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
